    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d695">

                <pb facs="0676" n="1410" sameAs="frus:frus1895p2/pg1410"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Terrell to Mr.
                            Olney.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the United States</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Constantinople</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1895-12-19"><hi rendition="#italic">December 19, 1895</hi></date>.
                        (Received Jan. 6, 1896.)</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 737.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have the honor to inclose herewith
                    delayed dispatches from Consul Jewett, Nos. 150 and 152, dated at Sivas on the
                    23d ultimo and 10th instant, which relate to the fearful condition of affairs in
                    Asia Minor.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">A. W. Terrell.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>




